Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "NighttimeParkingLotWithLowLighting" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :StateAnomaly ;
    :hasObstacle :obstacle1 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2, :risk3 .

:obstacle1 a :RoadObject ;
    :description "Poorly lit parking lot with structural beams obstructing view" .

:weather1 a :NightCondition .

:risk1 a :OcclusionRisk ;
    :description "Structural beams obstructing view of distant objects" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :RoadConditionRisk ;
    :description "Low lighting conditions in parking lot" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:risk3 a :CollisionRisk ;
    :description "Potential collision risk due to limited visibility of parked vehicles" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev3 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.60"^^xsd:float .

:sev3 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.80"^^xsd:float .

:vehicle1 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Parked vehicle in the distance" .
```

Identified Risks for each risk class:

**Risk 1:**
Description: Structural beams obstructing view of distant objects
Severity Score: 0.75

**Risk 2:**
Description: Low lighting conditions in parking lot
Severity Score: 0.60

**Risk 3:**
Description: Potential collision risk due to limited visibility of parked vehicles
Severity Score: 0.80

---
The scene is classified as a **StateAnomaly** due to the static but hazardous conditions (poor lighting and structural obstructions) that create risks without any dynamic behavior anomalies. The ontology does not include a specific class for "poor lighting," so it is mapped to **RoadConditionRisk** under the broader **Risk** class. The parked vehicle is included as an **Obstacle** of type **RoadObject** to reflect its potential collision risk.